- op: discuss  # 8ed9
  at: '2026-08-30T02:32:01Z'  # 8ed9
  by: agent  # 8ed9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8ed9
  clock: 7  # 8ed9
  nonce: 8ed9  # 8ed9
  message: "UNBLOCKED, with the tranche order CHANGED by the measurement. WI-vapud / measurement 0009 is done: the deferred-crossing family is NOT largely inert (45 of 62 rows measured in real idiom fire, 72.6%), so the retag moves real output and is worth doing. Three things it settled that bear directly on this item. (1) THIS ITEM'S OWN CASE IS NOW MEASURED ON A RUN. In an ordinary go accept loop -- net.Listen, ln.Accept(), conn.Read() -- the chains that come back are net/http.ListenAndServe, net.Listen, syscall.{Socket,Bind,Listen} and unix.{Socket,Bind,Listen}: EIGHT false setup sources. ln.Accept() and conn.Read() produce NOTHING. So go's entire net_recv surface on a real server is eight false sources and zero true receives, and ADR-0049 ruling 3's represented-crossing licence is satisfied by the retag itself rather than by the Accept/Read rows. Fixture: idiom/go2 in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/vapud_reach_08292026/. (2) TRANCHE ORDER. Go stdlib SETUP+LAUNCH fires completely and is the right first tranche. Go's seven THIRD-PARTY framework rows (gin/fiber/echo/grpc) are INERT in real code -- they are entered through constructor calls and blocked on WI-lalot -- so they go last; moving them changes no output and would make any A/B read a clean zero. (3) The register with per-row shape, which this item needs to cut tranches at all, is committed as the verdict table in docs/measurements/0009 and as verdict.json in the artifact dir."  # 8ed9
- op: discuss  # b317
  at: '2026-08-30T02:37:26Z'  # b317
  by: agent  # b317
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b317
  clock: 8  # b317
  nonce: b317  # b317
  message: "Starting the retag. Plan, in ADR-0049's terms: the 8 rows are DEFERRED CROSSINGS, so they are RETAGGED to net_listen, not REMOVED. That distinction is what dissolves this item's own F2 exemption rationale -- 'removing them takes go's network-input surface to nothing rather than relocating it' is true of removal and false of a retag, because a net_listen row still CLASSIFIES (so the call stays examined under INV-buzab) and its shadow qualifies any clean net_recv verdict rather than granting one. Tranche, from measurement 0009: go stdlib SETUP (net.Listen*, syscall/unix Socket/Bind/Listen) and LAUNCH (net/http.ListenAndServe*, Serve) FIRE in real idiom and are the payload; the seven third-party framework rows are inert pending WI-lalot and are retagged for correctness while being expected to change no output. Evidence bar per ADR-0049 ruling 3: a represented-crossing proof on a RUN, plus an INV-buzab false-all-clear check."  # b317
- op: discuss  # abcb
  at: '2026-08-30T02:47:45Z'  # abcb
  by: agent  # abcb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # abcb
  clock: 9  # abcb
  nonce: abcb  # abcb
  message: "RETAGGED. 11 rows moved from net_recv to net_listen: net.{Listen,ListenTCP,ListenUDP,ListenUnix,ListenPacket} and {syscall,unix}.{Socket,Bind,Listen}. THE MEASUREMENT, on the idiomatic accept-loop fixture (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/vapud_reach_08292026/idiom/go2): BEFORE 8 net_recv chains, net_listen_edges=0 -- every chain a setup or launch call, ZERO true receives. AFTER 7 net_listen + 1 net_recv, net_listen_edges=7. Every crossing still represented; nothing dropped. ADR-0049 ruling 3 met on a run. SCOPE NARROWED MID-CHANGE, and the reason is worth recording. I first moved 21 rows -- the setup rows PLUS every server-launch row (net/http.ListenAndServe*, Serve, gin.Run*, echo.Start*, fiber.Listen*, grpc.Serve). TestServerLaunchStaysAReceive went red on go/net/http.Serve, which is that pin doing exactly its job: its docstring makes the launch family's retag conditional on ADR-0049 open-work steps 1-4, and STEP 3 (adjudicated findings per shape) IS NOT DONE. Steps 1, 2 and 4 are (WI-hazop; WI-vapud/measurement 0009; the INV-buzab check re-proved end-to-end on the shipped catalogue). So the launch rows were reverted and this change is the SETUP rows only -- which is what this item's statement actually names. The launch-family retag needs step 3 and is not licensed yet. THE F2 EXEMPTION IS NOW ROW-LEVEL, NOT LANGUAGE-LEVEL, which is strictly narrower than what this item asked for. One offender survives the widened gate: github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2.App.Listen. It is a FALSE POSITIVE OF THE PREDICATE -- fiber's Listen blocks and serves, so it is launch rather than setup, and it is caught only because the predicate matches lowercase NAMES while the family is cut by MECHANISM. F2_EXEMPT_ROWS excuses that single (module, name) pair, a companion test fails if the row is ever retagged or removed, and the repro assertion now pins the EXACT remaining offender rather than asserting empty -- an empty assertion would have forced either a wrong retag or a language-wide skip, and both hide a row."  # abcb
