- op: discuss  # dbf4
  at: '2026-08-30T03:18:59Z'  # dbf4
  by: agent  # dbf4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dbf4
  clock: 11  # dbf4
  nonce: dbf4  # dbf4
  message: "SATISFIED. PR #640, merged as 51871f5edf, CI green. The statement -- 'No connection-SETUP call (socket/bind/listen) is declared net_recv in any catalogued language' -- now holds across all 15 catalogues with the widened, case-folded, tree-derived F2 gate enforcing it and NO language-level exemption for go. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, not a proxy. Re-ran this item's own repro on the merged tree: the 8 filed offenders are gone from net_recv. And the run-level check ADR-0049 ruling 3 demands, on an idiomatic go accept loop (net.Listen -> ln.Accept -> conn.Read): BEFORE 8 net_recv chains, every one a setup or launch call and ZERO true receives; AFTER 7 net_listen + 1 net_recv, net_listen_edges=7. Every crossing still represented, nothing dropped. End to end on the shipped catalogue, the same edge and claim that returned a bare confirmed now return confirmed_with_caveats naming the site -- so the retag did not buy a false all-clear (INV-buzab). ONE OFFENDER REMAINS AND IS NOT A SURVIVOR: github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2.App.Listen is a false positive of the F2 predicate, which matches lowercase NAMES while the family is cut by MECHANISM -- fiber's Listen blocks and serves. It is exempted at ROW granularity (F2_EXEMPT_ROWS), which is strictly narrower than the language-wide skip this item started with, and a companion test fails if the row is ever retagged or removed. It moves with the launch family. WHAT IS NOT DONE, STATED PLAINLY: the server-LAUNCH rows have not moved in ANY language. They are equally ADR-0049 deferred crossings and are pinned together across nine languages by TestServerLaunchStaysAReceive until ADR-0049 open-work STEP 3 (adjudicated findings per shape) clears. Steps 1, 2 and 4 are done. I initially moved all 21 rows; the pin went red and was right, and that is why this landed at 11."  # dbf4
